{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789459877,"nonce":"q8wlqSW1W1jxX2Bo36VOgERUdV4=","title":"Collector: the mapped-range probe assumed 16 KB pages","message":"`mapped()` aligned the probed range down to a 16 KB boundary before `msync`. On a 4 KB-page system (Linux, x86_64 macOS) a large block whose mapping starts at a 4 KB boundary was aligned into the page below it, `msync` answered ENOMEM, and the block was skipped as unmapped: nothing it held was marked. `crates/compiler/tests/collector.rs` caught it on the Linux and x86_64 macOS CI legs (32 bytes live where a megabyte was expected); on the aarch64 Mac every mapping is 16 KB aligned so it passed.\n\nFix: the page size comes from `sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE)`, read once.","files":null}]}